{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118032","id":3471562820,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7O69hE","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118032","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118032.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118032.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118032","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118032/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118032/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118032/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/8299b03c1a83092d9896ff4946f2c7943f744201","number":118032,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"GDScript: Fix type deduction for functions without `return` statements","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"* Fixes #118011.\r\n* Resolves #118007.\r\n\r\nPreviously, when a function's return type was unspecified, GDScript attempted to infer it based on the presence or absence of `return` statements in the function body (`Variant` or `void`). However, this is incorrect, since functions can be overridden in child classes, and abstract methods have no bodies at all. I think it's more correct to infer `Variant` in the case of an unspecified return type (or copy the return type from the parent method when overriding).\r\n\r\nThere is one subtle point. If you explicitly specify the `Variant` type (or it's copied from the parent method), you must return some value. However, if the return type isn't specified, you aren't required to return a value. This internal flag (`GDScriptParser::DataType::type_source`) is implicitly copied, but it's not distinguishable in `MethodInfo` reflection and documentation (`Variant` is used regardless of the presence or absence of the flag). However, I don't think we need to distinguish between these two options (#118007) - if a method returns a `Variant`, you can always use `return null` in code generation. In my opinion, the only problem is that reflection incorrectly reported the method as `void`.\r\n\r\nI'll also ignore for now the issue that GDScript sometimes treats `return` as `return null`. This can be somewhat complicated, which we can address later. See also https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/79363#pullrequestreview-1598144070.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godo